<title>USA: Argentine minister says no plans to hike diesel.</title>
<headline>Argentine minister says no plans to hike diesel.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Argentina's secretary of energy and ports, Alfredo Mirkin, said Tuesday that the government has no plans to raise domestic diesel prices.</p>
<p>Speaking at a New York seminar on investing in Argentina's energy sector, Mirking said of the government, &quot;we have no intention of raising diesel prices.&quot;</p>
<p>He said he did not know the basis for widespread reports in the Argentine press saying the government planned to raise domestic disel fuel prices.</p>
<p>((New York Energy Desk, +1 212 859 1620))</p>
